# PROPOSED — not yet a shipped deployment target. See
# docs/MOBILE_HOSTING_DECISIONS.md for the decision this file exists to
# make concrete evidence for, and core/database.py's docstring for why a
# SQLite DATABASE_URL is safe to use with this reduced dependency set.
#
# A trimmed variant of requirements.in for a resource-constrained,
# single-device, Docker-less host (the motivating case: a dedicated
# always-on Android tablet running this natively under Termux — see the
# decision doc above). Verified against the REAL test suite
# (tests/test_*.py, 2599 tests) with this exact file's packages installed
# and nothing else: 2597 passed, 2 skipped-by-design (a positive-control
# test for faster-whisper's import, which this profile deliberately never
# installs, and one test-harness env leak unrelated to this file). See
# docs/MOBILE_HOSTING_DECISIONS.md for the full verification record.
#
# Three things removed from requirements.in, each already gracefully
# optional in the application code (not a new capability, just not
# installing something the code already treats as best-effort):
#
#   - asyncpg — only reachable via a `postgresql+asyncpg://` DATABASE_URL;
#     this profile is meant to be paired with a `sqlite+aiosqlite://` one
#     instead. core/database.py's engine construction needed NO code
#     change for this — SQLAlchemy 2.x's async SQLite pool already accepts
#     the same pool_size/max_overflow kwargs the Postgres path uses.
#
#   - resemblyzer (and its hard `torch` dependency, ~500MB+ once its
#     transitive CUDA wheels resolve, or ~180MB even pinned to the
#     CPU-only build) — services/voice_auth.py already tries `from
#     resemblyzer import VoiceEncoder` and catches ImportError, falling
#     back to a librosa MFCC comparison ("reliable, no model download",
#     per that module's own docstring). Not installing it is choosing the
#     fallback deliberately, not disabling a feature — voice
#     identification still works, just via the second tier the code
#     already has.
#
#   - faster-whisper (and its ctranslate2 dependency) — only ever imported
#     when TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER=local (the app's own default, so this
#     profile MUST set TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER=openai or another cloud
#     provider explicitly in .env). See services/transcription.py's own
#     module docstring: "On 'openai' NOTHING imports faster_whisper."
#     Verified directly: with this file's packages and
#     TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER=openai, `sys.modules` contains no
#     faster_whisper, torch, or resemblyzer after a full app boot +
#     transcription preload() call.
#
# Everything else is identical to requirements.in — numpy/scipy/librosa/
# soundfile stay (voice_auth's MFCC fallback and services/transcription.py
# both need them regardless of which STT backend is chosen), as does every
# non-voice/non-DB dependency.
